fix(test): read the unit that carries the command, not the one that carries the clock

OPS-035 asserts the scheduled job gets a PATH that can find docker, because the
first install of this schedule fired on demand and wrote one line saying it
could not reach the stack. That assertion was reading the wrong file on Linux.

launchd puts the program, its arguments and its PATH in a single plist. systemd
splits them: the timer says WHEN and the service says WHAT and with which
environment. The test read the timer on both platforms, so on Linux it asserted
a PATH against a file that can never hold one, and printed the timer's text
while doing it.

It reads the service now, and the helper that picks the file says why the two
names differ rather than looking like a typo.

Checked the assertion still holds rather than merely moving: job_path always
seeds /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin and prepends wherever docker actually is,
so the file the test now reads does contain the directory it looks for.

